    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**What changed:**\n- Injected `HttpServletRequest` into the controller so the `addOwner` method can read the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (the method signature itself is fixed by the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface, so reading it from the request is the idiomatic way to get it without regenerating the contract).\n- Added a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer>` that records, per idempotency key, the id of the owner the first create produced.\n- In `addOwner`: when a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` is present and already seen, it looks up the original owner and returns it with **200 OK** (via the existing `toOwnerDto` mapping, with household member count populated) instead of running the create path \u2014 which would otherwise `409` on the duplicate-identity guard. On a first, unseen key, the owner is created normally (**201 Created**) and the key\u2192id mapping is recorded.\n\nThe new `replayIdempotentCreate` helper also gracefully falls through to a normal create if the remembered owner no longer exists.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` test (and the whole suite) passes: the first create returns 2xx, the repeat with the same key returns 200 with the same id.",
