    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:193`). I've marked each step as a **[validation]** (can reject the request) or a **[side-effect]** (mutates state/payload/logs).\n\n## Before the controller method runs\n\n1. **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 148). Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[validation] Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody` (`OwnersApi.java:86`), applied to `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`, `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters plus limited separators; lastName allows a trailing `.`).\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`.\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`.\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`.\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`.\n   - Failures produce `400`.\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (`@Transactional`)\n\n3. **[side-effect / short-circuit] Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key already produced an owner that still exists, returns `200 OK` with the original owner and **skips the entire create** (`replayIdempotentCreate`, lines 194\u2013200, 217\u2013228).\n\nThen `createOwner` (line 242) runs the rules **in this order**:\n\n### `normalizeAndValidate` (line 351)\n4. **[side-effect] Normalize address** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, recomposes the flat `address`, or normalizes the flat `address` and clears the structured fields; written back onto the payload (`normalizeAddress`, line 377).\n5. **[validation] Required fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank (after address normalization) \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (`validateRequiredFields`, line 503).\n6. **[validation] Postcode region rule** \u2014 if a postcode is present and the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), it must fall in that region's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (`validatePostcode`, line 531).\n7. **[side-effect] Normalize telephone** \u2014 converts to E.164 form and writes it back onto the payload (line 355\u2013356). (Invalid numbers that can't yield a valid E.164 value are rejected here.)\n8. **[validation] City capacity** \u2014 the city (case-insensitive) must hold fewer than 50 owners \u2192 `OwnerCityFullException` (`requireCityHasCapacity`, line 610).\n9. **[side-effect] Resolve registration date** \u2014 defaults to the server's current date when omitted; **[validation]** a supplied future date is rejected \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`; the date is then rolled forward off weekends/public holidays and written back onto the payload (`resolveRegistrationDate`, line 415).\n10. **[validation] Daily limit** \u2014 fewer than 100 owners may already carry that (adjusted) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (`requireDailyLimitNotReached`, line 439).\n11. **[side-effect] Normalize email** \u2014 lower-cased canonical form written back onto the payload (`normalizeEmail`, line 400).\n\n### Mapping and derived fields\n12. **[side-effect] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner` (line 244; `id`, `pets`, `deleted` ignored).\n13. **[side-effect] Populate derived fields** (`populateDerivedFields`, line 302), in order:\n    - `customerCode` \u2014 derived then de-duplicated against existing owners with a `-n` suffix (`deriveUniqueCustomerCode`, line 319).\n    - `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), snapshot before save.\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 `true` if >80 owners already exist for that day.\n    - `householdId` \u2014 derived from last name + postcode (null when no postcode).\n\n### Duplicate guards\n14. **[validation] Unique identity** \u2014 the derived `identityKey` (normalized telephone + email + householdId) must not match any non-deleted existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (`requireUniqueIdentity`, line 556).\n15. **[validation] Household not duplicate** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, no other non-deleted owner may already belong to this `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (`requireHouseholdNotDuplicate`, line 651).\n16. **[side-effect] Flag possible (soft) duplicate** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a different phone (skipped if `sharesHousehold=true` or no postcode) (`flagPossibleDuplicate`, line 581).\n\n### Persist and finish\n17. **[side-effect] Save the owner** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` persists it and assigns its id (line 249).\n18. **[side-effect] Populate household member count** \u2014 sets the transient `householdMemberCount` (line 250).\n19. **[side-effect] Audit log** \u2014 one line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber (`auditOwnerCreated`, line 280).\n20. **[side-effect] Store idempotency mapping** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records key \u2192 new owner id (lines 202\u2013204).\n21. **[side-effect] Build `201 Created` response** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (which itself derives salutation, displayName, initials, checkDigit, membershipNumber, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/Level, locality, timezone, telephoneDisplay, contactPreference, ageBand, selfLink) and stamps the `identityKey`, plus a `Location` header pointing at `/api/owners/{id}` (`createdOwnerResponse`/`toOwnerDto`, lines 263, 184).\n\nNote: v2 (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) only exposes a paged `GET`; creation is exclusively the v1 endpoint above."
